### Result Output

Only commands declared with `with_result: true` expose result output options.

Result output modes:

- `human`: the default; renders the result through the normal logger
- `json`: writes machine-readable JSON
- `yaml`: writes machine-readable YAML

Nil results are treated as successful execution with no result to emit.

Result output and logging combinations:

| `output_format` | `output_file` | Allowed `logger` values | Behaviour | Allowed |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `human` | empty or `-` | `console`, `plain`, `rich`, `json`, `quiet`, `file`, `none`, `custom` | The result is rendered through the configured logger on the normal logger stream. | yes |
| `human` | any file path | none | `output_file` is rejected because human output does not use the machine-readable file/output stream. | no |
| `json` or `yaml` | empty or `-` | `console`, `plain`, `rich`, `json`, `quiet`, `file`, `none`, `custom` | The machine-readable result is written to standard output. `logger=console`, `logger=plain`, `logger=rich`, `logger=json`, and `logger=quiet` are accepted but normal logging is routed away from stdout so the result stream stays clean. | yes |
| `json` or `yaml` | any file path | `console`, `plain`, `rich`, `json`, `quiet`, `file`, `none`, `custom` | The machine-readable result is written to the selected file and normal logging follows the configured logger mode. | yes |

`logger=file` still requires `logger_file` in every allowed combination.

`--output-file` is only valid when `--output-format` is `json` or `yaml`.

When `--output-file=-` is used, the command writes to standard output.

When `--output-format=json` or `--output-format=yaml` is selected without `--output-file`, stdout is reserved for the machine-readable result. Normal logging and annotations are routed away from stdout so shell composition remains reliable.

When machine-readable result output is written to standard output, the command accepts `logger=file`, `logger=custom`, or `logger=none`. This prevents standard console logging from colliding with the machine-readable result stream.

When `--output-format=human` is selected, the result is rendered through the logger and there is no dedicated machine-readable stdout stream.

